> but I was wrong.  Wasted some skill slots on that one.

On the one hand, a short sword's base damage is
significantly better than a dagger's, so even though the
artifact bonus for Orcrist is wimpy, it's still a rather
better melee weapon than a dagger, all else being equal.

Of course, all else is not equal, because roles that can
get to Expert in dagger should always do so.  Putting
skill points into dagger is seldom a waste, because
you're going to be using them as projectiles anyway.

In your case, the +4 enchantment on the dagger is
also relevant.  In the early game, that's quite a
good enchantment.

Of course, you'd eventually be wanting to trade up to
something with better base damage, such as a longsword.

